# --- The book itself. Never commit these. --------------------------------------
# The repository is public. 04_..._Full_Book_Digital_Mobile.pdf is the complete
# 64-page book; putting it here would publish for free the one thing the whole
# project treats as scarce (CLAUDE.md, non-negotiable 7). The other three are the
# print-ready covers and interior — supplier files, not web files.
#
# tools/extract_book_content.py reads these to generate src/content/**. That
# generated content IS committed, so the site builds from a fresh clone. Only
# re-running the extraction needs the PDFs, and that is a job for this machine.
/*.pdf

# --- Camera originals -----------------------------------------------------------
# ~40MB of unprocessed shoots, most of them a 13-year-old. The six photographs the
# site actually uses are curated, cropped and re-encoded in src/assets/photos/, and
# Astro's image pipeline strips EXIF on the way out. The originals do not: the
# Zolder frame still carries GPS coordinates and a timestamp. Publishing raw
# originals of a minor is exactly what CLAUDE.md rules out.
/IMG_*.jpg
/IMG_*.jpeg
/image000*.jpeg
/era-round-*.jpg
/Ontwerp zonder titel*.png
/judge-*.jpeg

# --- Working material -----------------------------------------------------------
# 36MB of review screenshots and design explorations. Useful while building, noise
# in a repository someone clones to run the site.
/design/

# --- Build output and tooling ---------------------------------------------------
node_modules/
dist/
.astro/
.playwright-mcp/
.vercel/
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.log
npm-debug.log*
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Local agent scratch, not project config (.claude/settings.json and
# .claude/skills/ are committed on purpose — they are how this repo is worked on).
.claude/scheduled_tasks.lock
.og-tmp.html
.review/
